      },
      {
       "text": "A dark state is a superposition of the metastable states that is not coupled to the excited state.",
       "src": "7.3"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{H}{\\kH} = \\mk{R}{-\\kOmegaone\\left(|2\\rangle\\langle 1| + |1\\rangle\\langle 2|\\right) - \\kOmegathree\\left(|2\\rangle\\langle 3| + |3\\rangle\\langle 2|\\right) - \\kOmegafour\\left(|2\\rangle\\langle 4| + |4\\rangle\\langle 2|\\right)}",
      "src": "7.3",
      "uses": [0]
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{H}{\\kH(a_1|1\\rangle + a_3|3\\rangle + a_4|4\\rangle)} = \\mk{R}{-(\\kOmegaone a_1 + \\kOmegathree a_3 + \\kOmegafour a_4)|2\\rangle}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "Acting on a state of the metastable levels: every term that ends in $\\langle 2|$ gives zero."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{R}{\\kOmegaone a_1 + \\kOmegathree a_3 + \\kOmegafour a_4} = \\mk{z}{0}",
       "uses": [
        1
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "step": 0
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{R}{\\kOmegaone a_1 + \\kOmegathree a_3 + \\kOmegafour a_4} = \\mk{z}{0}",
      "uses": []
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{R}{\\kOmegathree a_3 + \\kOmegafour a_4} = \\mk{z}{0}",
